1
00:00:00,100 --> 00:00:02,560
[Disclaimer: Characters, behaviors,
places, organizations, professions,

2
00:00:02,580 --> 00:00:05,040
and events shown
in the series are entirely fictional,

3
00:00:05,060 --> 00:00:07,520
solely for the purpose of entertainment,
with no intention to instruct

4
00:00:07,540 --> 00:00:10,000
or promote any kind of behavior;
viewer discretion is advised]

5
00:00:10,200 --> 00:00:12,480
Try wearing the day's lucky color.

6
00:00:14,390 --> 00:00:15,480
Dressed in all green, huh?

7
00:00:15,600 --> 00:00:17,920
Guess you won't need
that inhaler anymore, huh?

8
00:00:18,160 --> 00:00:20,800
You can just get a desk lamp.

9
00:00:21,010 --> 00:00:23,240
It'll bring you luck in love.

10
00:00:23,350 --> 00:00:24,600
Can you guarantee that?

11
00:00:24,900 --> 00:00:27,000
You have my word as Xinxin,
the feng shui master.

12
00:00:27,210 --> 00:00:28,360
You're still single, then?

13
00:00:28,510 --> 00:00:29,500
Hey...

14
00:00:29,520 --> 00:00:30,640
are you trying to fish for info?

15
00:00:30,790 --> 00:00:32,290
What do you think about...

16
00:00:32,700 --> 00:00:34,240
people who like the same sex?

17
00:00:34,330 --> 00:00:37,300
People just fall in love with someone.

18
00:00:37,990 --> 00:00:39,920
It's not a sin or anything.

19
00:00:42,640 --> 00:00:45,160
[JR CONSTRUCTION]

20
00:00:45,820 --> 00:00:48,410
You can contact the contractor
for Mr. Mongkol's project now.

21
00:00:48,600 --> 00:00:49,400
Alright.

22
00:00:49,910 --> 00:00:51,450
- We closed the deal perfectly.
- Exactly.

23
00:00:51,470 --> 00:00:52,890
Structural design and drafts

24
00:00:52,910 --> 00:00:54,310
have all been approved,
no feng shui master needed.

25
00:00:55,410 --> 00:00:56,580
Well, we did rely on one.

26
00:00:57,410 --> 00:00:58,190
How so?

27
00:00:59,010 --> 00:01:02,080
I consulted Xinxin about the feng shui.

28
00:01:03,200 --> 00:01:03,790
What?

29
00:01:04,870 --> 00:01:05,390
But...

30
00:01:05,670 --> 00:01:07,280
you two were still
fighting that day, weren't you?

31
00:01:07,500 --> 00:01:10,310
I thought you couldn't work on
the same project anymore.

32
00:01:10,700 --> 00:01:13,320
Or has our architect finally opened up
to the feng shui master?

33
00:01:13,510 --> 00:01:14,960
Aha...

34
00:01:16,010 --> 00:01:17,920
I just wanted to
get this work done quickly.

35
00:01:18,180 --> 00:01:19,510
Opened up what?

36
00:01:19,530 --> 00:01:20,790
Who would believe in that kind of stuff?

37
00:01:20,820 --> 00:01:21,820
Such nonsense.

38
00:01:24,320 --> 00:01:25,520
- Oh?
- What?

39
00:01:27,000 --> 00:01:28,390
- Let's go.
- I'm lost.

40
00:01:28,600 --> 00:01:29,990
Don't forget to contact
Mr. Mongkol, alright?

41
00:01:30,010 --> 00:01:30,680
Alright.

42
00:01:33,360 --> 00:01:33,970
[Sloth Sukiyaki]

43
00:01:33,990 --> 00:01:36,900
So, what should we have today?

44
00:01:37,710 --> 00:01:39,240
How about sukiyaki?

45
00:01:39,800 --> 00:01:41,400
That way,
you'll actually eat some veggies.

46
00:01:42,510 --> 00:01:43,590
Mom!

47
00:01:43,610 --> 00:01:45,040
I do eat them, you know.

48
00:01:45,120 --> 00:01:47,290
You barely eat any, though.

49
00:01:47,310 --> 00:01:48,680
I eat some, though.

50
00:01:48,700 --> 00:01:49,410
Come on.

51
00:01:50,180 --> 00:01:50,900
This one, alright?

52
00:01:51,600 --> 00:01:53,120
Oh? Auntie Tai!

53
00:01:53,600 --> 00:01:54,730
Xinxin.

54
00:01:54,750 --> 00:01:56,130
Hello, Auntie Tai.

55
00:01:56,150 --> 00:01:57,920
- Hello.
- Are you here to shop?

56
00:01:57,940 --> 00:01:58,890
That's right.

57
00:01:58,910 --> 00:02:00,660
I was bored,
so I came out for a bit today.

58
00:02:00,680 --> 00:02:02,080
Soul is here, too.

59
00:02:02,100 --> 00:02:03,610
She'll be here in a minute.

60
00:02:03,630 --> 00:02:04,240
Oh.

61
00:02:04,980 --> 00:02:06,600
Uh, this is...

62
00:02:06,720 --> 00:02:08,020
Phing,

63
00:02:08,040 --> 00:02:09,080
my mom.

64
00:02:09,100 --> 00:02:10,510
And this is...

65
00:02:10,530 --> 00:02:11,620
Auntie Tai,

66
00:02:11,640 --> 00:02:12,610
Soul's mom.

67
00:02:12,630 --> 00:02:13,380
Oh...

68
00:02:13,410 --> 00:02:14,710
- Hello.
- Hello.

69
00:02:14,730 --> 00:02:15,920
What did you just call me?

70
00:02:18,120 --> 00:02:19,120
Hello, Auntie Phing.

71
00:02:19,140 --> 00:02:20,810
Hi.

72
00:02:23,400 --> 00:02:24,890
Are you in a rush?

73
00:02:24,920 --> 00:02:26,650
Do you want to grab some food together?

74
00:02:26,670 --> 00:02:29,690
Actually, we were just
about to go have sukiyaki.

75
00:02:29,710 --> 00:02:30,540
I see.

76
00:02:30,560 --> 00:02:33,370
That's great. We're looking for
something to eat, too.

77
00:02:33,400 --> 00:02:36,270
Then please join us.
I was thinking of having sukiyaki,

78
00:02:36,290 --> 00:02:38,410
since this one
doesn't really eat vegetables.

79
00:02:38,430 --> 00:02:39,560
I see...

80
00:02:39,590 --> 00:02:42,120
Mine just loves to eat vegetables.

81
00:02:42,370 --> 00:02:44,430
I sometimes joke that she's like a cow

82
00:02:44,460 --> 00:02:46,360
- with a fridge full of veggies and grass.
- Mom!

83
00:02:48,040 --> 00:02:48,590
Right.

84
00:02:48,610 --> 00:02:50,410
Then please join us, Ms. Tai.

85
00:02:50,430 --> 00:02:51,620
- Alright.
- Be my guest.

86
00:02:51,640 --> 00:02:52,820
Thank you for letting us join, Ms. Phing.

87
00:02:52,840 --> 00:02:54,170
- It's my pleasure.
- Right.

88
00:02:54,190 --> 00:02:55,780
- Come on, let's get inside, dear.
- Let's go.

89
00:02:55,800 --> 00:02:56,830
Alright.

90
00:02:56,850 --> 00:02:58,920
She eats so few vegetables,
so I thought...

91
00:02:59,410 --> 00:03:00,560
I don't think what you said

92
00:03:00,580 --> 00:03:02,030
worked out very well,

93
00:03:02,060 --> 00:03:03,540
since we've kept

94
00:03:03,560 --> 00:03:04,570
running into each other.

95
00:03:05,500 --> 00:03:07,990
I guess my energy is running low.

96
00:03:08,010 --> 00:03:09,820
I think it's time to make some merit.

97
00:04:47,310 --> 00:04:48,660
Make sure you eat plenty of vegetables,

98
00:04:48,680 --> 00:04:50,900
especially carrots, dear.

99
00:04:50,920 --> 00:04:53,670
Because they have vitamins
that are good for your eyes.

100
00:04:53,690 --> 00:04:55,030
Since you're a feng shui master,

101
00:04:55,050 --> 00:04:57,510
you must use your eyes a lot, right?

102
00:04:58,180 --> 00:05:01,690
But I'm a feng shui master,
not a rabbit, Mom.

103
00:05:01,820 --> 00:05:04,010
If you make me eat this much,

104
00:05:04,210 --> 00:05:06,110
I'll just dig a hole and live in it.

105
00:05:07,110 --> 00:05:08,420
They are just the same.

106
00:05:08,530 --> 00:05:10,810
Soul used to hate vegetables
when she was little.

107
00:05:10,830 --> 00:05:12,640
I think when she was seven,

108
00:05:12,660 --> 00:05:16,510
she hid some broccoli under the couch

109
00:05:16,530 --> 00:05:19,050
and left it there
until it rotted and smelled awful.

110
00:05:19,080 --> 00:05:21,640
It's a good thing
her habits changed as she grew up.

111
00:05:22,710 --> 00:05:23,590
Mom.

112
00:05:23,610 --> 00:05:25,310
That was over 20 years ago.

113
00:05:25,330 --> 00:05:27,900
Why'd you say that?
You're embarrassing me.

114
00:05:27,920 --> 00:05:29,240
It's true, though.

115
00:05:29,500 --> 00:05:31,590
I didn't know you had this in you.

116
00:05:31,610 --> 00:05:33,700
I thought you were a nerdy kid

117
00:05:33,720 --> 00:05:35,680
who'd been holding
a steel ruler since day one.

118
00:05:38,400 --> 00:05:40,120
Hey, Ms. Tai.

119
00:05:40,310 --> 00:05:42,370
My girl is also something else.

120
00:05:42,390 --> 00:05:44,610
When she was around ten,

121
00:05:44,630 --> 00:05:47,350
- Right.
- she started believing in horoscopes and stuff.

122
00:05:47,500 --> 00:05:50,210
We went to the temple to see a monk,

123
00:05:50,500 --> 00:05:53,320
and he said she'd have some bad luck.

124
00:05:53,610 --> 00:05:55,240
She really believed what he said,

125
00:05:55,260 --> 00:05:57,810
so she locked herself
in a room for three whole days.

126
00:05:57,830 --> 00:06:00,980
I had to leave food and water
outside her room.

127
00:06:01,000 --> 00:06:02,960
It was like having a kuman thong at home.

128
00:06:05,100 --> 00:06:07,680
That's called faith, Mom.

129
00:06:08,260 --> 00:06:10,280
I just followed the advice I got.

130
00:06:10,300 --> 00:06:11,880
Right, faith, you say.

131
00:06:11,900 --> 00:06:14,440
Alright, faith it is.

132
00:06:15,100 --> 00:06:16,370
Hey, Ms. Tai.

133
00:06:16,390 --> 00:06:18,400
Is Soul...

134
00:06:18,600 --> 00:06:20,290
dating anyone right now?

135
00:06:20,820 --> 00:06:21,620
Oh?

136
00:06:22,060 --> 00:06:23,520
She's single now.

137
00:06:24,110 --> 00:06:26,090
But when she loves someone,

138
00:06:26,320 --> 00:06:28,600
she puts all her cards on the table.

139
00:06:29,030 --> 00:06:30,060
Back then,

140
00:06:30,080 --> 00:06:33,440
she wanted to knit someone a scarf.

141
00:06:33,590 --> 00:06:36,490
She didn't even know
how to knit, but she learned.

142
00:06:36,650 --> 00:06:37,730
And then

143
00:06:37,750 --> 00:06:39,600
she came back
with a three-meter-long scarf.

144
00:06:39,620 --> 00:06:41,320
I thought it was a naga!

145
00:06:41,340 --> 00:06:42,150
Gosh!

146
00:06:42,170 --> 00:06:45,240
Was that meant to go around
the neck or the whole body?

147
00:06:45,760 --> 00:06:46,800
Auntie Phing.

148
00:06:47,340 --> 00:06:48,780
Since Xinxin

149
00:06:49,040 --> 00:06:52,100
has believed in horoscopes
and lucky colors since childhood,

150
00:06:52,120 --> 00:06:54,030
I wonder what color she wore

151
00:06:54,050 --> 00:06:55,680
for her university entrance exam.

152
00:06:57,130 --> 00:06:59,960
Vermilion was the lucky color that day.

153
00:07:00,500 --> 00:07:02,030
And guess what she did?

154
00:07:02,510 --> 00:07:04,160
Her undershirt was vermilion,

155
00:07:04,180 --> 00:07:06,700
so were her jacket and pants.

156
00:07:06,720 --> 00:07:08,100
Even her bow was in vermilion.

157
00:07:08,120 --> 00:07:10,460
But I think she was lucky
the color of the day

158
00:07:10,480 --> 00:07:12,480
wasn't the three-colored spirit cloth.

159
00:07:12,500 --> 00:07:13,860
Otherwise, she'd become...

160
00:07:13,880 --> 00:07:16,210
a guardian spirit of that room.

161
00:07:16,900 --> 00:07:18,420
Mom!

162
00:07:18,440 --> 00:07:20,010
Actually, I have another story to tell.

163
00:07:20,030 --> 00:07:22,670
- About the wealth-attracting ritual.
- Ugh, stop it!

164
00:07:23,190 --> 00:07:24,190
Moms,

165
00:07:24,690 --> 00:07:27,860
let's stop talking about
our childhood antics for now,

166
00:07:27,880 --> 00:07:29,711
because this meatball
is about to explode.

167
00:07:29,716 --> 00:07:30,960
This lava-filled one.

168
00:07:30,980 --> 00:07:32,290
- Come on, have some.
- Let's dig in.

169
00:07:32,590 --> 00:07:33,780
I know you're hangry.

170
00:07:50,910 --> 00:07:52,440
You're only checking out my profile.

171
00:07:52,810 --> 00:07:54,500
I don't think that's fair.

172
00:07:55,000 --> 00:07:55,580
Uh...

173
00:08:01,050 --> 00:08:02,100
Your Instagram account.

174
00:08:03,100 --> 00:08:03,820
Alright.

175
00:08:09,920 --> 00:08:10,920
Here you go.

176
00:08:15,640 --> 00:08:16,520
[Following]

177
00:08:17,760 --> 00:08:19,510
[lada_stories_ started following you]

178
00:08:19,530 --> 00:08:20,660
[Follow back]

179
00:08:20,680 --> 00:08:22,000
[Following]

180
00:08:26,390 --> 00:08:28,120
I'm sorry I'm late.

181
00:08:28,710 --> 00:08:32,310
I got a little lost because
I don't come around here very often.

182
00:08:32,900 --> 00:08:34,070
It's fine.

183
00:08:34,090 --> 00:08:36,200
I just got here.

184
00:08:37,690 --> 00:08:39,180
I ordered this for you.

185
00:08:39,310 --> 00:08:41,120
I thought you might be hungry.

186
00:08:41,600 --> 00:08:44,600
How did you know what I wanted?

187
00:08:46,200 --> 00:08:49,320
Well, you look mixed-race.

188
00:08:50,720 --> 00:08:52,600
Actually, I like Thai food.

189
00:08:55,060 --> 00:08:56,300
Uh, but...

190
00:08:56,940 --> 00:08:59,280
but I like what you ordered more.

191
00:09:01,600 --> 00:09:04,000
You almost gave me a heart attack.

192
00:09:04,820 --> 00:09:08,100
I actually guessed from looking at
your lifestyle on Instagram.

193
00:09:09,590 --> 00:09:10,590
Thank you.

194
00:09:12,910 --> 00:09:16,560
How about we talk about work while we eat?

195
00:09:17,100 --> 00:09:18,240
I think we shouldn't.

196
00:09:18,500 --> 00:09:19,660
I'm free today,

197
00:09:20,800 --> 00:09:23,000
and my whole day is yours.

198
00:09:35,540 --> 00:09:36,990
What should we do now?

199
00:09:37,510 --> 00:09:40,700
It's gonna take hours for them
to finish getting their nails done.

200
00:09:47,840 --> 00:09:48,720
Come with me.

201
00:09:54,620 --> 00:09:56,600
Where are you taking me?

202
00:10:01,880 --> 00:10:03,910
To get you a lamp, of course.

203
00:10:03,930 --> 00:10:06,100
I know you won't believe me.

204
00:10:06,320 --> 00:10:08,800
It's not like I want
to be in love that much anyway.

205
00:10:10,180 --> 00:10:11,690
It wouldn't hurt, you know.

206
00:10:11,820 --> 00:10:13,800
So you won't be this stiff.

207
00:10:30,510 --> 00:10:31,890
I'll buy it for you.

208
00:10:31,910 --> 00:10:34,200
Consider it a good-luck charm
from a feng shui master.

209
00:10:35,600 --> 00:10:36,360
I don't want it.

210
00:10:36,610 --> 00:10:38,110
I don't want to owe anyone.

211
00:10:39,610 --> 00:10:40,520
How much?

212
00:10:40,690 --> 00:10:41,920
I'll pay you back.

213
00:10:42,710 --> 00:10:43,300
Oh.

214
00:10:43,600 --> 00:10:45,160
How's Mr. Mongkol's project going?

215
00:10:45,280 --> 00:10:46,410
You haven't told me anything.

216
00:10:46,430 --> 00:10:47,760
Are you even listening?

217
00:10:47,980 --> 00:10:48,780
Heard it.

218
00:10:48,800 --> 00:10:49,620
Got it.

219
00:10:49,910 --> 00:10:51,820
So, how's the project?

220
00:10:52,540 --> 00:10:53,800
It's going well.

221
00:10:54,030 --> 00:10:55,560
Mr. Mongkol is happy with it.

222
00:10:56,100 --> 00:10:57,810
Thank you for your help.

223
00:10:58,960 --> 00:11:01,320
Then I should get something in return.

224
00:11:18,220 --> 00:11:20,100
Isn't this a bit modest of you?

225
00:11:23,100 --> 00:11:26,680
Honestly,
I don't really need much in life.

226
00:11:26,900 --> 00:11:27,870
First,

227
00:11:27,900 --> 00:11:28,600
money.

228
00:11:29,190 --> 00:11:30,040
Second,

229
00:11:30,690 --> 00:11:32,280
sweets and delicious food.

230
00:11:40,400 --> 00:11:41,400
Don't you want some?

231
00:11:42,330 --> 00:11:43,210
No, I don't.

232
00:11:43,310 --> 00:11:44,710
I'm not a fan of sweets.

233
00:11:45,070 --> 00:11:45,920
Whoa...

234
00:11:46,790 --> 00:11:48,110
How boring of you.

235
00:11:50,660 --> 00:11:52,390
I just care about my health.

236
00:11:53,400 --> 00:11:54,120
Alright.

237
00:11:54,710 --> 00:11:55,310
Well...

238
00:11:55,970 --> 00:11:57,480
You don't eat sweets,

239
00:11:57,740 --> 00:11:59,880
you don't eat fried food,

240
00:11:59,900 --> 00:12:01,600
and even your light bulbs
come in odd numbers.

241
00:12:02,320 --> 00:12:03,920
And a foul mouth...

242
00:12:04,890 --> 00:12:06,320
I mean, sharp-tongued.

243
00:12:06,610 --> 00:12:07,290
Mm.

244
00:12:07,310 --> 00:12:10,410
That's why love will never find you.

245
00:12:10,520 --> 00:12:11,900
It's only going to run away.

246
00:12:12,710 --> 00:12:15,600
Seriously, after everything you just said,

247
00:12:15,800 --> 00:12:18,120
would love ever come running to me?

248
00:12:19,310 --> 00:12:20,310
It would.

249
00:12:20,560 --> 00:12:22,600
And it's not coming slowly.

250
00:12:23,070 --> 00:12:24,670
It's running at pace one.

251
00:12:24,690 --> 00:12:26,220
You won't even see it coming.

252
00:12:53,100 --> 00:12:56,800
Is she afraid people won't know
it's a love-boosting lamp?

253
00:13:17,520 --> 00:13:18,520
Excuse me, boss.

254
00:13:18,910 --> 00:13:20,200
I was tied up with a client just now.

255
00:13:20,510 --> 00:13:21,190
It's alright.

256
00:13:21,900 --> 00:13:22,900
Here, come on in.

257
00:13:27,220 --> 00:13:27,990
Alright.

258
00:13:28,100 --> 00:13:29,100
Shall we get started, then?

259
00:13:30,110 --> 00:13:32,360
Could you share what tasks
you're currently working on?

260
00:13:32,670 --> 00:13:33,590
Let's start with Soul.

261
00:13:33,610 --> 00:13:36,400
I'm currently handling four projects.

262
00:13:36,610 --> 00:13:37,490
Mm...

263
00:13:37,510 --> 00:13:38,710
That's quite a lot to take on.

264
00:13:40,000 --> 00:13:40,760
What about you, Pat?

265
00:13:41,490 --> 00:13:42,910
I have two.

266
00:13:43,720 --> 00:13:44,630
Okay.

267
00:13:44,770 --> 00:13:46,800
Now we have a new project coming in.

268
00:13:47,210 --> 00:13:48,490
It's for Madam Waen,

269
00:13:48,510 --> 00:13:49,900
our regular client.

270
00:13:50,680 --> 00:13:53,520
She's planning to build
a vacation home in Pran Buri.

271
00:13:53,690 --> 00:13:55,910
Actually, I'm thinking of
assigning this project to Soul

272
00:13:56,680 --> 00:13:59,010
since you've worked with her before

273
00:13:59,030 --> 00:14:00,210
and probably know her well.

274
00:14:00,710 --> 00:14:02,510
But I've already mentioned to her that

275
00:14:02,820 --> 00:14:04,300
Soul might be busy.

276
00:14:05,020 --> 00:14:07,590
In that case, just assign it to Pat.

277
00:14:08,600 --> 00:14:09,950
You can handle this, right?

278
00:14:11,490 --> 00:14:13,451
Normally, I limit myself to three projects

279
00:14:13,463 --> 00:14:14,290
because...

280
00:14:14,720 --> 00:14:15,720
I...

281
00:14:16,040 --> 00:14:17,900
can't give them all enough attention.

282
00:14:19,100 --> 00:14:22,500
But if Soul can handle
four projects this well...

283
00:14:23,400 --> 00:14:24,400
I guess I can take it on, then.

284
00:14:25,420 --> 00:14:26,420
Okay.

285
00:14:26,930 --> 00:14:28,690
So, your team will be responsible for

286
00:14:28,710 --> 00:14:30,020
Madam Waen's project, alright?

287
00:14:31,300 --> 00:14:33,710
But Madam is quite particular
about feng shui,

288
00:14:34,010 --> 00:14:36,490
so you might have to work closely
with the feng shui master.

289
00:14:37,130 --> 00:14:38,500
Mm... I'm alright with that.

290
00:14:39,120 --> 00:14:40,900
Who is that feng shui master, by the way?

291
00:14:41,200 --> 00:14:42,200
I might know them.

292
00:14:43,310 --> 00:14:44,750
It's probably the same one.

293
00:14:45,810 --> 00:14:47,400
She has her own feng shui master.

294
00:14:48,220 --> 00:14:49,070
Boss,

295
00:14:49,090 --> 00:14:51,120
could you assign me to this project?

296
00:14:53,000 --> 00:14:54,120
Are you sure?

297
00:14:54,790 --> 00:14:56,850
You already have too much work.
I don't think you can manage.

298
00:14:57,910 --> 00:14:59,010
I can do it.

299
00:15:01,000 --> 00:15:03,120
With the team leader being this stubborn,

300
00:15:03,250 --> 00:15:05,190
if the client ends up complaining,

301
00:15:05,500 --> 00:15:06,850
we'll all be in trouble.

302
00:15:08,620 --> 00:15:11,100
That has never happened to me,

303
00:15:11,600 --> 00:15:13,100
and it never will.

304
00:15:21,900 --> 00:15:23,110
Is Miss Architect in charge

305
00:15:23,130 --> 00:15:25,010
of this project, Madam Waen?

306
00:15:25,390 --> 00:15:26,510
Yes, she is.

307
00:15:26,530 --> 00:15:29,900
At first, the company was gonna
send some handsome guy.

308
00:15:29,920 --> 00:15:31,900
But I don't know what she was thinking.

309
00:15:31,920 --> 00:15:33,880
In the room, she offered

310
00:15:34,020 --> 00:15:36,090
to have her team take on this project.

311
00:15:36,110 --> 00:15:39,910
I think she might want to work with you.

312
00:15:40,290 --> 00:15:42,090
Does she want to work with me,

313
00:15:42,110 --> 00:15:44,300
or is she just messing with my head?

314
00:15:44,700 --> 00:15:46,420
Oh, come on...

315
00:15:46,440 --> 00:15:47,700
Trust me,

316
00:15:47,720 --> 00:15:49,320
my dear feng shui master.

317
00:15:49,420 --> 00:15:53,050
You two have great chemistry
when you work together.

318
00:15:53,190 --> 00:15:54,100
I can feel

319
00:15:54,120 --> 00:15:57,420
the energy whenever you argue.

320
00:15:57,440 --> 00:15:59,910
It really livens up my house.

321
00:16:00,490 --> 00:16:02,450
Maybe it's spiteful energy?

322
00:16:02,480 --> 00:16:03,170
Oh, come on...

323
00:16:03,396 --> 00:16:05,646
Whatever that energy is,

324
00:16:05,670 --> 00:16:06,711
the deposit has already been transferred

325
00:16:06,933 --> 00:16:09,686
to the company.

326
00:16:09,711 --> 00:16:13,570
I hope you two will nail this project.

327
00:16:13,590 --> 00:16:17,590
Because I believe in both Xinxin,
the feng shui master, and Ms. Soul.

328
00:16:19,000 --> 00:16:19,690
Alright.

329
00:16:23,420 --> 00:16:25,500
Gotta pray for good fortune ASAP.

330
00:16:29,210 --> 00:16:31,600
What will my relationship with her be like?

331
00:16:35,100 --> 00:16:37,520
[THE LOVERS]

332
00:16:40,560 --> 00:16:42,190
Oh, no way...

333
00:16:47,890 --> 00:16:49,000
Soul...

334
00:16:49,020 --> 00:16:51,050
I've already taken it. What can I do?

335
00:16:51,070 --> 00:16:54,510
I thought you said Madam Waen's
project traumatized you.

336
00:16:54,530 --> 00:16:56,600
Why did you take on
another project for her?

337
00:16:56,620 --> 00:16:57,670
She's right.

338
00:16:57,780 --> 00:16:59,920
Both Madam Waen and that feng shui lady.

339
00:16:59,940 --> 00:17:01,610
You can't stand either of them.

340
00:17:01,630 --> 00:17:03,040
Then why did you do this?

341
00:17:03,200 --> 00:17:04,310
Go ahead, yell at me.

342
00:17:04,330 --> 00:17:06,080
Don't hold back.

343
00:17:06,100 --> 00:17:07,360
Oh, we won't.

344
00:17:07,380 --> 00:17:08,340
You'd just yell back at us!

345
00:17:08,860 --> 00:17:11,230
But you have to tell us your plan

346
00:17:11,450 --> 00:17:13,940
- and how you intend to handle it.
- Yeah.

347
00:17:13,960 --> 00:17:16,000
Or do you just want to
pick a fight with Pat?

348
00:17:16,140 --> 00:17:16,610
Uh...

349
00:17:17,080 --> 00:17:17,720
Well...

350
00:17:18,200 --> 00:17:20,100
Pat was getting on my nerves first.

351
00:17:20,190 --> 00:17:22,070
He said I couldn't handle the projects.

352
00:17:22,090 --> 00:17:24,390
How could I just let him
talk down to me like that?

353
00:17:24,410 --> 00:17:25,110
Mm...

354
00:17:25,920 --> 00:17:26,920
I get it now.

355
00:17:26,940 --> 00:17:28,300
It was Pat, right?

356
00:17:28,590 --> 00:17:29,210
Okay.

357
00:17:29,400 --> 00:17:30,840
How could he do this to us?

358
00:17:30,870 --> 00:17:33,460
We need to start a war over this.

359
00:17:33,480 --> 00:17:34,490
We'd better show them

360
00:17:34,510 --> 00:17:37,010
that our team is the best in the company!

361
00:17:37,890 --> 00:17:40,520
Oyl, you're acting like
you got insulted yourself.

362
00:17:41,530 --> 00:17:42,530
Mm.

363
00:17:42,700 --> 00:17:44,000
This is unacceptable.

364
00:17:44,790 --> 00:17:45,790
Mm.

365
00:17:49,210 --> 00:17:51,310
How did you end up here?

366
00:17:52,560 --> 00:17:54,100
About Madam Waen's project,

367
00:17:54,430 --> 00:17:55,710
have you accepted it yet?

368
00:17:56,500 --> 00:17:57,500
I already have.

369
00:17:58,420 --> 00:18:01,010
Did you know I was the one in charge?

370
00:18:01,450 --> 00:18:02,380
I knew.

371
00:18:02,690 --> 00:18:03,690
And you still took it?

372
00:18:04,510 --> 00:18:06,090
Why shouldn't I?

373
00:18:06,380 --> 00:18:08,920
I can work with any architect,

374
00:18:08,940 --> 00:18:10,220
and they pay me well, too.

375
00:18:10,310 --> 00:18:11,310
What about you?

376
00:18:11,400 --> 00:18:13,210
Why did you take it on?
Haven't you learned your lesson?

377
00:18:15,800 --> 00:18:16,410
Well...

378
00:18:17,390 --> 00:18:18,020
Well...

379
00:18:19,100 --> 00:18:19,970
They pay me well.

380
00:18:20,100 --> 00:18:20,720
Yeah,

381
00:18:21,390 --> 00:18:22,390
they pay me well.

382
00:18:22,960 --> 00:18:25,070
So it turns out
you're all about the money, too.

383
00:18:26,600 --> 00:18:28,810
Of course I want money when I work.

384
00:18:29,120 --> 00:18:30,450
If not for money,

385
00:18:30,470 --> 00:18:31,820
then what for?

386
00:18:32,510 --> 00:18:33,690
Well, for me.

387
00:18:35,220 --> 00:18:37,960
I thought you wanted to work with me.

388
00:18:38,130 --> 00:18:39,670
I bet arguing with other feng shui masters

389
00:18:39,690 --> 00:18:41,400
isn't as fun as arguing with me.

390
00:18:43,870 --> 00:18:45,510
I don't even need to argue

391
00:18:45,610 --> 00:18:47,080
with other feng shui masters.

392
00:18:49,110 --> 00:18:50,910
Here you go,

393
00:18:50,930 --> 00:18:52,810
spicy pork leg tom yum.

394
00:18:55,690 --> 00:18:56,610
Look.

395
00:18:56,770 --> 00:18:59,050
Uh... I made chive dumplings.

396
00:18:59,080 --> 00:19:00,680
Take some home for your mom too, okay?

397
00:19:00,700 --> 00:19:02,110
Oh, alright.

398
00:19:04,290 --> 00:19:05,600
Here you go.

399
00:19:09,000 --> 00:19:10,790
Come on. Let's eat.

400
00:19:12,000 --> 00:19:13,090
Thank you.

401
00:19:18,910 --> 00:19:20,450
Come on, let's dig in.

402
00:19:24,580 --> 00:19:26,930
You grow quite fast, though.

403
00:19:35,400 --> 00:19:37,410
Why don't you go home
after you've eaten?

404
00:19:38,110 --> 00:19:40,300
I'm waiting for your mom's chive dumplings.

405
00:19:41,910 --> 00:19:43,130
Do you like plants?

406
00:19:43,910 --> 00:19:44,510
Well...

407
00:19:45,310 --> 00:19:46,510
not that much.

408
00:19:46,740 --> 00:19:48,090
I just help my mom take care of them.

409
00:19:50,130 --> 00:19:52,310
So, do you know all of them?

410
00:19:53,490 --> 00:19:54,690
Go ahead, ask me.

411
00:19:57,810 --> 00:19:58,520
This one.

412
00:19:58,890 --> 00:20:00,180
Crown of thorns.

413
00:20:00,400 --> 00:20:01,310
How about this one?

414
00:20:01,410 --> 00:20:02,440
Tulip.

415
00:20:03,010 --> 00:20:04,020
Tulip?

416
00:20:05,590 --> 00:20:07,270
That's a dracaena!

417
00:20:10,820 --> 00:20:12,360
And this one?

418
00:20:14,390 --> 00:20:16,510
I get not knowing the others,

419
00:20:16,910 --> 00:20:18,340
but this one's a golden pothos.

420
00:20:18,610 --> 00:20:19,800
You really don't know?

421
00:20:20,310 --> 00:20:21,320
I know.

422
00:20:21,520 --> 00:20:22,910
I just want to know

423
00:20:22,930 --> 00:20:25,700
if it's the same as the one
you told me to put on my desk.

424
00:20:25,810 --> 00:20:26,810
That's all.

425
00:20:27,190 --> 00:20:27,920
It is.

426
00:20:28,590 --> 00:20:29,590
Did you put it there yet?

427
00:20:32,240 --> 00:20:33,110
Not yet.

428
00:20:33,520 --> 00:20:34,400
I knew it.

429
00:20:34,730 --> 00:20:37,000
You don't listen to a word I say.

430
00:20:38,010 --> 00:20:41,170
It's not that I don't care,
but I don't have time to buy it.

431
00:20:56,060 --> 00:20:56,810
Here,

432
00:20:56,910 --> 00:20:57,690
you can have it.

433
00:21:00,750 --> 00:21:01,750
A golden pothos is so easy

434
00:21:01,770 --> 00:21:03,530
to take care of, you know?

435
00:21:03,790 --> 00:21:06,300
It can grow in both soil and water.

436
00:21:06,500 --> 00:21:07,950
If you can't keep it alive,

437
00:21:08,300 --> 00:21:10,120
you shouldn't bother
trying anything else in this lifetime.

438
00:21:11,510 --> 00:21:12,510
I know, I know.

439
00:21:12,800 --> 00:21:14,790
I'll take really good care of it.

440
00:21:14,990 --> 00:21:16,800
Do I need to tuck it in as well?

441
00:21:18,500 --> 00:21:19,610
Does it get cold easily?

442
00:22:02,960 --> 00:22:03,810
Hey.

443
00:22:06,070 --> 00:22:06,910
Hey!

444
00:22:11,220 --> 00:22:12,220
Hey, you!

445
00:22:15,040 --> 00:22:16,500
What's wrong with you?!

446
00:22:18,300 --> 00:22:21,570
I'm not driving
just so you can sleep comfortably.

447
00:22:21,590 --> 00:22:23,270
Can't you stay awake with me?

448
00:22:23,400 --> 00:22:24,750
Well, I'm bored!

449
00:22:24,770 --> 00:22:26,340
What do you want me to do?

450
00:22:26,360 --> 00:22:27,960
I can't even drive.

451
00:22:29,290 --> 00:22:31,100
But you have a car, don't you?

452
00:22:35,190 --> 00:22:36,590
It's someone else's car.

453
00:22:37,800 --> 00:22:39,110
I'm just keeping it for them.

454
00:23:07,120 --> 00:23:08,900
Did Madam Waen arrange
to meet us at the temple?

455
00:23:09,980 --> 00:23:10,980
No, she didn't.

456
00:23:11,490 --> 00:23:13,090
We still have some time left,

457
00:23:13,110 --> 00:23:15,690
so I brought you here to pray first.

458
00:23:16,920 --> 00:23:17,920
You brought me?

459
00:23:18,300 --> 00:23:19,010
Mm.

460
00:23:19,410 --> 00:23:22,900
You were just complaining
about having low energy lately.

461
00:23:22,920 --> 00:23:24,390
You need to make merit, don't you?

462
00:23:24,900 --> 00:23:25,600
Well,

463
00:23:26,030 --> 00:23:26,890
we're here now.

464
00:23:28,290 --> 00:23:30,130
Since when do you
pay attention to what I say?

465
00:23:32,710 --> 00:23:33,360
Uh...

466
00:23:33,730 --> 00:23:35,100
We still have some time,

467
00:23:35,130 --> 00:23:36,620
and it's on the way,

468
00:23:36,640 --> 00:23:38,130
so I thought we'd stop by.

469
00:23:39,010 --> 00:23:39,910
That's all.

470
00:23:39,930 --> 00:23:41,290
Oh...

471
00:23:41,320 --> 00:23:42,360
Come on, get out.

472
00:23:52,590 --> 00:23:53,590
Here.

473
00:24:05,900 --> 00:24:06,530
Come on.

474
00:24:26,710 --> 00:24:27,890
What are you looking at?

475
00:24:28,520 --> 00:24:30,100
Nothing. Just...

476
00:24:30,320 --> 00:24:32,010
You seem really focused.

477
00:24:33,660 --> 00:24:34,660
Well...

478
00:24:34,680 --> 00:24:36,850
I just hope our project goes smoothly

479
00:24:36,870 --> 00:24:39,200
and I don't lose my mind in the process...

480
00:24:39,560 --> 00:24:40,260
Okay?

481
00:24:43,320 --> 00:24:44,590
I'm just joking.

482
00:24:44,800 --> 00:24:48,240
I believe that if you come to pray,
you must do it from the heart.

483
00:24:48,440 --> 00:24:50,290
You shouldn't rush or anything.

484
00:24:50,600 --> 00:24:51,600
Hm...

485
00:24:51,860 --> 00:24:54,290
I usually see you relying on feng shui.

486
00:24:54,720 --> 00:24:56,490
I didn't think you'd visit temples much.

487
00:24:57,020 --> 00:24:59,510
Actually, someone told me that

488
00:24:59,530 --> 00:25:00,600
feng shui is about

489
00:25:00,620 --> 00:25:02,410
organizing the external environment.

490
00:25:02,760 --> 00:25:06,480
But if you don't organize
your mind and body well,

491
00:25:06,620 --> 00:25:08,690
even if you place the fountain
in the right direction,

492
00:25:08,710 --> 00:25:10,110
you'll still be hot-tempered.

493
00:25:10,790 --> 00:25:11,910
Hm...

494
00:25:13,530 --> 00:25:14,880
Who taught you that?

495
00:25:15,410 --> 00:25:16,410
That's a good lesson.

496
00:25:16,950 --> 00:25:17,700
Dad...

497
00:25:21,500 --> 00:25:22,800
Someone, I guess.

498
00:25:25,240 --> 00:25:26,490
A long time ago.

499
00:25:41,400 --> 00:25:42,610
Let's make a wish first.

500
00:25:42,640 --> 00:25:43,710
Alright.

501
00:25:43,790 --> 00:25:44,570
Come on.

502
00:25:50,410 --> 00:25:52,070
Let's go.

503
00:25:52,700 --> 00:25:54,800
Look at you go, little one.

504
00:25:55,100 --> 00:25:57,100
Don't get caught like this again, alright?

505
00:26:03,100 --> 00:26:04,390
Here you go.

506
00:26:05,010 --> 00:26:06,010
I'll hold it for you.

507
00:26:06,130 --> 00:26:07,130
Here.

508
00:26:07,800 --> 00:26:09,000
Let's see.

509
00:26:11,200 --> 00:26:12,490
Whoa!

510
00:26:12,900 --> 00:26:14,810
- So many of them.
- So many of them!

511
00:26:17,100 --> 00:26:18,170
- Oh?!
- That one is orange.

512
00:26:18,190 --> 00:26:19,700
The orange fish!

513
00:26:19,790 --> 00:26:20,930
Must be a salmon.

514
00:26:25,110 --> 00:26:26,110
Let me put it here.

515
00:26:26,600 --> 00:26:27,670
Okay.

516
00:26:27,700 --> 00:26:29,280
I have to throw it far out.

517
00:26:29,620 --> 00:26:30,620
Get into position first.

518
00:26:31,100 --> 00:26:31,830
Look here.

519
00:26:31,850 --> 00:26:33,090
Whoa, whoa, whoa.

520
00:26:33,600 --> 00:26:35,520
That didn't go any farther!

521
00:26:35,960 --> 00:26:36,810
Come on,

522
00:26:36,840 --> 00:26:37,840
look here.

523
00:26:37,860 --> 00:26:39,980
- I'll show you how to make it go farther.
- Hey!

524
00:26:40,590 --> 00:26:41,710
Oh, that's not far either.

525
00:26:43,290 --> 00:26:44,700
Go, go.

526
00:26:47,100 --> 00:26:48,320
There are so many of them.

527
00:26:53,920 --> 00:26:54,990
We're out of food now.

528
00:26:55,210 --> 00:26:56,410
Do you want more?

529
00:26:57,480 --> 00:26:58,480
I'd better get going.

530
00:27:25,350 --> 00:27:26,710
Come on, wake up.

531
00:27:30,750 --> 00:27:31,710
Hey.

532
00:27:32,500 --> 00:27:33,500
Wake up.

533
00:27:43,210 --> 00:27:45,990
Can't I sleep a little more?

534
00:27:48,620 --> 00:27:49,800
Hey!

535
00:27:49,820 --> 00:27:51,110
Wake up!

536
00:27:59,340 --> 00:28:00,490
We're here already?

537
00:28:03,200 --> 00:28:05,060
Driving's so tiring, huh.

538
00:28:08,920 --> 00:28:09,920
Mm...

539
00:28:10,420 --> 00:28:11,720
The same room?!

540
00:28:12,160 --> 00:28:13,790
Yes, because you only booked one.

541
00:28:14,830 --> 00:28:16,230
I have no problem with that.

542
00:28:17,310 --> 00:28:18,700
But I do!

543
00:28:18,890 --> 00:28:19,370
Huh?

544
00:28:19,640 --> 00:28:21,010
So what do you want?

545
00:28:23,510 --> 00:28:25,300
Are there really no rooms available?

546
00:28:25,820 --> 00:28:28,190
We're completely booked.
I truly apologize for the inconvenience.

547
00:28:28,800 --> 00:28:29,800
Hey, you.

548
00:28:29,940 --> 00:28:31,730
Madam Waen booked this

549
00:28:31,750 --> 00:28:33,130
and even paid for it.

550
00:28:33,260 --> 00:28:35,420
We're here to work,
not on vacation, alright?

551
00:28:35,440 --> 00:28:37,100
Just sleep wherever they put you.

552
00:28:37,950 --> 00:28:40,210
But I don't want to sleep
in the same room as you.

553
00:28:40,720 --> 00:28:41,610
What's your problem?

554
00:28:41,630 --> 00:28:43,300
We're both women.

555
00:28:43,320 --> 00:28:44,610
What are you scared of anyway?

556
00:28:46,110 --> 00:28:47,110
Of course I'd be scared.

557
00:28:47,650 --> 00:28:49,560
You're a lady-killer.

558
00:28:52,960 --> 00:28:54,670
Uh, please go ahead with that.

559
00:28:54,960 --> 00:28:55,840
Hey!

560
00:29:07,530 --> 00:29:09,120
We have to sleep in the same bed?

561
00:29:10,310 --> 00:29:12,110
It's pretty big.

562
00:29:12,140 --> 00:29:13,610
I don't mind.

563
00:29:13,960 --> 00:29:15,350
But I do mind!

564
00:29:23,490 --> 00:29:24,550
Then you take

565
00:29:24,810 --> 00:29:25,810
the right side

566
00:29:26,010 --> 00:29:27,780
and I'll take the left.

567
00:29:28,110 --> 00:29:29,010
That's fine by me.

568
00:29:29,570 --> 00:29:31,180
Hurry and catch up when you're done.

569
00:29:31,200 --> 00:29:32,400
I'll wait in the car.

570
00:29:32,430 --> 00:29:33,800
It's almost time.

571
00:29:40,600 --> 00:29:41,600
Ugh...

572
00:29:41,920 --> 00:29:43,090
What the heck?!

573
00:29:43,610 --> 00:29:45,400
This must be Madam Waen's doing!

574
00:29:52,760 --> 00:29:55,690
Hello, Ms. Soul
and Feng Shui Master Xinxin.

575
00:29:55,710 --> 00:29:57,760
- Hello, Madam Waen.
- Hello.

576
00:29:57,780 --> 00:29:59,720
How's the room? Is it okay?

577
00:30:00,510 --> 00:30:04,310
It's okay, but I thought
we'd get a private room.

578
00:30:04,430 --> 00:30:05,560
Oh...

579
00:30:05,580 --> 00:30:08,680
I thought you wouldn't mind
sharing a room since you seem so close.

580
00:30:08,760 --> 00:30:11,410
I'm sorry for not asking you first.

581
00:30:12,510 --> 00:30:13,970
It's alright, but...

582
00:30:13,990 --> 00:30:16,560
if there's a next time,
I'd prefer a separate room.

583
00:30:16,780 --> 00:30:17,460
Uh...

584
00:30:17,480 --> 00:30:20,560
I think we should start
before it gets dark.

585
00:30:21,140 --> 00:30:22,480
Alright. Let's go.

586
00:30:22,590 --> 00:30:24,170
Come on, I'll show you over there.

587
00:30:24,200 --> 00:30:25,200
Follow me.

588
00:30:26,490 --> 00:30:27,700
Right here, right here.

589
00:30:28,880 --> 00:30:30,580
The plot is here

590
00:30:30,600 --> 00:30:32,930
and goes all the way there.

591
00:30:32,950 --> 00:30:34,150
Whoa.

592
00:30:34,320 --> 00:30:35,490
- Alright, alright.
- Yes.

593
00:30:35,520 --> 00:30:37,360
What do you think of this location?

594
00:30:37,440 --> 00:30:38,440
It's really nice.

595
00:30:38,460 --> 00:30:39,800
It faces the sea

596
00:30:39,900 --> 00:30:41,250
and is backed by mountains.

597
00:30:41,400 --> 00:30:44,510
It'll bring prosperity to both
your business and your fortune.

598
00:30:44,600 --> 00:30:46,580
It's good for your health, too.

599
00:30:46,600 --> 00:30:47,770
That's good to hear.

600
00:30:47,790 --> 00:30:51,410
But you shouldn't build the house
too close to the sea.

601
00:30:51,500 --> 00:30:53,210
Strong winds could batter it,

602
00:30:53,230 --> 00:30:56,200
and the salty sea air
could make you uncomfortable.

603
00:30:56,400 --> 00:30:57,400
I see.

604
00:30:58,510 --> 00:30:59,920
That's why

605
00:30:59,940 --> 00:31:02,120
the house needs to be built
some distance from the sea.

606
00:31:02,180 --> 00:31:03,560
- Mm, alright.
- Hey, you.

607
00:31:03,600 --> 00:31:05,700
But not so far away
that the breeze can't reach it.

608
00:31:13,610 --> 00:31:14,990
There's one more thing, Madam.

609
00:31:15,010 --> 00:31:16,000
What is it?

610
00:31:16,320 --> 00:31:18,160
No piling is allowed here.

611
00:31:18,360 --> 00:31:19,790
Oh...

612
00:31:19,950 --> 00:31:21,280
What are you talking about?

613
00:31:21,980 --> 00:31:24,520
Build a house without driving piles?
Are you out of your mind?!

614
00:31:24,930 --> 00:31:26,280
- What were you thinking?
- Uh...

615
00:31:26,370 --> 00:31:27,910
Hold on, Ms. Soul.

616
00:31:27,930 --> 00:31:28,920
Well...

617
00:31:28,960 --> 00:31:30,580
Actually, I don't

618
00:31:30,600 --> 00:31:33,320
stay here very often.
I only come here once in a while.

619
00:31:33,380 --> 00:31:35,160
I think it would be alright without piling.

620
00:31:35,200 --> 00:31:36,200
I'm afraid not.

621
00:31:36,220 --> 00:31:36,900
Uh...

622
00:31:36,930 --> 00:31:37,880
Hey,

623
00:31:37,900 --> 00:31:39,180
she said it's alright.

624
00:31:39,200 --> 00:31:41,300
Do you ever think about her safety?

625
00:31:42,260 --> 00:31:42,940
Uh...

626
00:31:42,960 --> 00:31:44,790
Hold on, hold on.

627
00:31:44,810 --> 00:31:46,910
Shall we wrap it up for today

628
00:31:46,930 --> 00:31:48,480
and continue it tomorrow?

629
00:31:48,540 --> 00:31:49,660
I'm getting tired,

630
00:31:49,690 --> 00:31:51,290
and the sky is getting dark, too.

631
00:31:51,310 --> 00:31:52,100
Let's go.

632
00:31:52,170 --> 00:31:54,080
Let's go before it rains.

633
00:31:54,140 --> 00:31:56,090
- Come on. Right? Come.
- A storm is coming.

634
00:32:00,310 --> 00:32:01,400
We need to talk

635
00:32:01,870 --> 00:32:03,210
when we get back.

636
00:32:07,800 --> 00:32:08,800
Ouch!

637
00:32:09,600 --> 00:32:10,600
Hey...

638
00:32:11,210 --> 00:32:12,280
It hurts!

639
00:32:12,420 --> 00:32:13,420
Let go of me!

640
00:32:14,510 --> 00:32:15,840
Are you messing with me?

641
00:32:16,510 --> 00:32:17,710
What did I do?

642
00:32:17,730 --> 00:32:19,220
The pile foundation!

643
00:32:19,520 --> 00:32:20,960
I meant it.

644
00:32:21,520 --> 00:32:23,400
But that's the main structure of the house.

645
00:32:23,420 --> 00:32:25,280
How is it supposed to stand without piling?

646
00:32:25,300 --> 00:32:27,000
Do you want it to float in the air?

647
00:32:27,200 --> 00:32:28,974
This is the real working world,

648
00:32:28,989 --> 00:32:30,080
not a playground

649
00:32:30,140 --> 00:32:31,880
for your childish games of revenge!

650
00:32:32,310 --> 00:32:34,240
But the client
chose to believe a kid like me.

651
00:32:34,380 --> 00:32:37,200
Because feng shui masters like you
completely ruined my work.

652
00:32:37,350 --> 00:32:40,710
I have to keep revising it nonstop
because of your careless words!

653
00:32:40,730 --> 00:32:42,100
I'm not careless!

654
00:32:42,780 --> 00:32:44,400
What if the house collapses?

655
00:32:44,900 --> 00:32:46,700
Will you share the responsibility with me?

656
00:32:47,060 --> 00:32:49,710
Or are you gonna say
it's because I didn't believe you?

657
00:32:51,390 --> 00:32:52,810
What kind of person are you?

658
00:32:52,830 --> 00:32:54,920
Do you want to look mystical
so people worship

659
00:32:54,940 --> 00:32:57,040
and bow down to you?

660
00:32:57,200 --> 00:32:58,890
You're just a fortune teller,

661
00:32:58,910 --> 00:33:00,720
not an engineer or an architect.

662
00:33:00,910 --> 00:33:02,980
What would you know about structures?

663
00:33:03,510 --> 00:33:05,960
Can you stop sticking your nose in?!

664
00:33:06,790 --> 00:33:08,900
Does having a degree

665
00:33:09,000 --> 00:33:10,930
give you the right to look down on me?

666
00:33:11,500 --> 00:33:14,620
Just because you've got a degree,

667
00:33:14,640 --> 00:33:17,510
my words mean nothing to you, right?

668
00:34:32,610 --> 00:34:34,100
"I just don't like rain."

669
00:35:00,800 --> 00:35:02,040
Xinxin!

670
00:35:03,330 --> 00:35:04,520
Xinxin!

671
00:35:10,070 --> 00:35:11,510
Xinxin!

672
00:35:20,600 --> 00:35:21,700
Xinxin!

673
00:35:24,490 --> 00:35:25,610
Xinxin!

674
00:35:26,420 --> 00:35:27,680
Xinxin!

675
00:35:31,390 --> 00:35:32,880
Xinxin!

676
00:35:49,920 --> 00:35:51,310
I'm sorry.

677
00:35:54,310 --> 00:35:55,910
It's okay now.

678
00:35:58,210 --> 00:35:59,210
I'm sorry.

679
00:36:49,800 --> 00:36:51,920
I'm sorry for...

680
00:36:52,910 --> 00:36:54,160
being so harsh.

681
00:36:58,970 --> 00:37:01,820
Well, you were right, though.

682
00:37:04,220 --> 00:37:06,290
I'm just a feng shui master.

683
00:37:08,200 --> 00:37:09,810
I only have belief,

684
00:37:10,990 --> 00:37:12,400
not knowledge.

685
00:37:14,510 --> 00:37:17,130
I didn't mean it that way.

686
00:37:17,150 --> 00:37:18,400
I just...

687
00:37:18,830 --> 00:37:22,000
I just didn't want you to
interfere with my project,

688
00:37:23,210 --> 00:37:26,220
but I forgot that it's your job, too.

689
00:37:29,920 --> 00:37:31,240
I'm sorry.

690
00:37:33,110 --> 00:37:34,000
Mm.

691
00:37:34,320 --> 00:37:35,840
I'm...

692
00:37:36,700 --> 00:37:38,320
sorry, too.

693
00:37:40,410 --> 00:37:43,040
I'm sorry for focusing only on my own work

694
00:37:45,700 --> 00:37:48,590
without caring how it affected you.

695
00:37:56,420 --> 00:37:57,550
Well,

696
00:37:57,570 --> 00:37:59,700
we still have to work together after all.

697
00:38:01,020 --> 00:38:02,020
I will

698
00:38:02,120 --> 00:38:05,210
handle the structural work,

699
00:38:06,300 --> 00:38:07,490
and you can just

700
00:38:07,920 --> 00:38:09,800
focus on the feng shui like before.

701
00:38:10,320 --> 00:38:11,160
Is that alright with you?

702
00:38:13,120 --> 00:38:14,210
I...

703
00:38:15,510 --> 00:38:17,310
wouldn't dare boss you around.

704
00:38:20,310 --> 00:38:22,280
You don't have to tell me what to do.

705
00:38:22,700 --> 00:38:24,610
Just remind me, that's all.

706
00:38:51,110 --> 00:38:52,610
I want to ask you something.

707
00:38:53,800 --> 00:38:54,800
Why...

708
00:38:55,800 --> 00:38:58,100
are you so scared of rain?

709
00:39:04,000 --> 00:39:06,420
It's alright
if you don't want to talk about it.

710
00:39:14,400 --> 00:39:15,210
I...

711
00:39:16,510 --> 00:39:19,510
once waited for my dad
to pick me up from school.

712
00:39:59,480 --> 00:40:00,840
I waited until it started raining,

713
00:40:03,000 --> 00:40:04,310
but he didn't show up.

714
00:40:12,710 --> 00:40:14,240
By the time Mom came to pick me up,

715
00:40:18,720 --> 00:40:21,160
I was already asleep there.

716
00:40:23,900 --> 00:40:25,390
After that...

717
00:40:28,390 --> 00:40:30,920
I never waited for that man again.

718
00:40:35,100 --> 00:40:36,890
That's why you're so scared of rain.

719
00:40:40,200 --> 00:40:42,040
Every time it rains,

720
00:40:46,030 --> 00:40:48,300
it reminds me of that day.

721
00:40:50,610 --> 00:40:52,500
I was scared,

722
00:40:53,720 --> 00:40:55,010
cold,

723
00:40:56,010 --> 00:40:57,500
and lonely.

724
00:41:01,620 --> 00:41:05,110
Maybe it's not the rain.

725
00:41:07,090 --> 00:41:09,720
Maybe it's the fear

726
00:41:10,610 --> 00:41:13,280
of having nothing to protect you.

727
00:41:20,570 --> 00:41:22,200
You may be right.

728
00:41:25,720 --> 00:41:28,800
I guess I have to keep finding
shelter from rain like this.

729
00:41:32,720 --> 00:41:34,920
Things won't stay
that way forever, you know.

730
00:41:36,110 --> 00:41:37,390
One day,

731
00:41:37,510 --> 00:41:39,710
you'll find your own umbrella, Xinxin.

732
00:41:40,930 --> 00:41:43,310
No matter how hard it rains,

733
00:41:46,120 --> 00:41:47,790
you won't need to find shelter.

734
00:41:55,390 --> 00:41:57,600
It's not because the rain has gone away,

735
00:41:59,450 --> 00:42:00,800
but because you...

736
00:42:02,020 --> 00:42:03,680
won't be scared of it anymore.

737
00:42:26,320 --> 00:42:27,210
Xinxin.

738
00:42:29,930 --> 00:42:30,990
Are you asleep yet?

739
00:42:32,900 --> 00:42:34,080
Not yet.

740
00:42:37,690 --> 00:42:38,990
Can I ask you something?

741
00:42:41,080 --> 00:42:42,080
What is it?

742
00:42:44,390 --> 00:42:46,440
When will you call me like that again?

743
00:42:49,480 --> 00:42:50,210
Well...

744
00:42:51,200 --> 00:42:53,100
I don't need to

745
00:42:53,120 --> 00:42:54,610
since we're just coworkers.

746
00:42:56,190 --> 00:42:58,640
But you said it the other day.

747
00:43:01,390 --> 00:43:01,980
Well...

748
00:43:02,910 --> 00:43:05,090
that was because the moms were with us.

749
00:43:06,610 --> 00:43:07,520
Okay.

750
00:43:08,100 --> 00:43:09,020
That's fine.

751
00:43:10,740 --> 00:43:12,080
It's okay if you don't.

752
00:43:29,930 --> 00:43:31,010
Are you asleep yet?

753
00:43:32,200 --> 00:43:34,690
Yeah, I'm gonna sleep now.

754
00:43:42,800 --> 00:43:43,800
Sweet dreams.

755
00:44:11,310 --> 00:44:13,110
You used to tell me...

756
00:44:13,360 --> 00:44:16,680
love will find its way to me
before I even realize it, right?

757
00:44:16,910 --> 00:44:18,160
I think...

758
00:44:18,510 --> 00:44:19,920
it's getting closer.

759
00:44:22,400 --> 00:44:23,920
You really don't realize

760
00:44:24,190 --> 00:44:25,560
I'm into you?

761
00:44:25,810 --> 00:44:27,040
I know.

762
00:44:27,560 --> 00:44:29,110
You're so obvious.

763
00:44:29,290 --> 00:44:31,080
You two are a couple, right?

764
00:44:31,100 --> 00:44:32,100
We are.

765
00:44:52,700 --> 00:44:53,880
Hey, what is it?!

766
00:44:53,960 --> 00:44:54,720
A snake!

767
00:44:54,740 --> 00:44:55,670
- Snake?!
- Snake!

768
00:44:55,690 --> 00:44:57,080
It bit me!

769
00:45:01,920 --> 00:45:03,200
A green one, too.

770
00:45:05,390 --> 00:45:07,040
Is it a green pit viper?

771
00:45:07,330 --> 00:45:08,440
I guess not.

772
00:45:08,900 --> 00:45:10,230
Not a green pit viper?

773
00:45:10,250 --> 00:45:11,690
Not a snake.

774
00:45:11,720 --> 00:45:12,680
Open your eyes.

775
00:45:19,620 --> 00:45:20,810
Are you scared of snakes?

776
00:45:21,400 --> 00:45:23,300
Who wouldn't be?

777
00:45:25,760 --> 00:45:26,850
Let's go.

778
00:45:26,870 --> 00:45:28,490
It's so overgrown around here.

779
00:45:29,130 --> 00:45:29,750
Mm.

780
00:45:29,910 --> 00:45:30,910
Alright.

781
00:45:32,610 --> 00:45:33,720
I'm coming with you.
